\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lol}{\contentsline {lstlisting}{code/max\textendash semantics.c}{4}{lstlisting.-3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:semantics}{{2}{4}{Existing C lane interpretations, with their QCP annotations omitted for space. The helpers inspect binary32 bit patterns and compare non-NaN values. Decimal constants \texttt {4194304U} and \texttt {2143289344U} encode the quiet-NaN bit and a canonical quiet NaN. The original definitions and contracts accompany the excerpts. The modeled Arm profile disables flush-to-zero and default-NaN behavior; floating-point exception flags are outside the output observation}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\def\@LN@column{1}
\newlabel{fig:vmax-performance}{{3}{5}{Preliminary local Saturn RTL measurements on finite inputs, reproduced from the archived experiment. Speed is XNNPACK RVV u8v cycles divided by the measured implementation's cycles. Each size uses one warm-up and the median of three timed calls within one simulation run; no confidence interval is claimed. Hardware VLEN is 512 bits and datapath width is 256 bits. The published optimized and XNNPACK implementations do not preserve the NEON NaN behavior; the repair adds that behavior. These are measurements, not proof results or a precise reproduction of the SALTyRN paper's configuration}{figure.caption.3}{}}
